BYTE STUB -- NOT A REAL TARBALL.

The failure-injection test in this repository needs a payload whose FILE NAME matches
the declared version, because the builder refuses to ship an older payload silently.
It never opens this file; a real deployment keeps its real tarballs out of the
repository (see .gitignore) and this stub stands in for them.

Name shape matters: a scoped package packs as "<scope>-<name>-<version>.tgz", so the
builder matches "*dsh-memory-*.tgz" rather than "dsh-memory-*.tgz". A narrower filter
silently misses every fresh download.
